  "body": "## What changed\n\nIt adds `cavity_outline` to Sinker Burn parameters.\nThe points use coordinates relative to the burn point.\nThe project file, operation digest and MCP tools carry the outline.\nAn empty outline keeps the previous extent law.\n\nThe size law compares the electrode with inward cavity wall offsets.\nIt permits the derived diamond finish electrode.\nIt still refuses an oversized electrode by name.\nIt also refuses malformed outlines, contradictory dimensions and an incomplete finish.\nCommand creation checks the outline and its stated dimensions.\nGeneration repeats the bounds checks.\nThe existing scalar law keeps the floor and condition checks.\n\nThe MCP schema declares an optional array with a `null` default.\nThe electrode reply supplies an array for a body and `null` for a rectangle.\nA `null` params patch clears the outline.\nThe independent stock verdict still checks the actual burn.\nTwo legacy-extent tests generate box burns and check the corner gouges.\n\nThe undercut stock check uses exact disc-polygon intersection.\nIt blocks a plunge or retract when the cutter head meets a stock corner.\nThe lollipop profile draws the full ball united with the neck.\n\n## UI screenshots\n\nThese inherited parent renders use the headless `ShellUi` (`1440x960` WGPU).\nThe before views show upstream `5ed5b7fe2`.\nThe after views come from parent PR #2714.\nThe pictured UI files are unchanged in #2836.\nThe images are stored only on `mkinney/Camcraft` branch `pr-screenshots`, at commit `0fd64401cc4acd068a1ec9e048417002176a3f86`:\n\n| View | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tool editor (`DT-20-60` dovetail cutter) | ![Tool editor before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0fd64401cc4acd068a1ec9e048417002176a3f86/2714/tool-editor-before.png) | ![Tool editor after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0fd64401cc4acd068a1ec9e048417002176a3f86/2714/tool-editor-after.png) |\n| Slot Undercut page (`TSlot` in milling setup) | ![Slot Undercut before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0fd64401cc4acd068a1ec9e048417002176a3f86/2714/slot-undercut-before.png) | ![Slot Undercut after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0fd64401cc4acd068a1ec9e048417002176a3f86/2714/slot-undercut-after.png) |\n\n## Cause\n\nThe previous law judged X and Y extents.\nAn inward offset moves a sharp diamond corner farther than the condition's undersize.\nThe correct finish electrode then failed the extent check.\nThe original pin reported a burned X extent of `19.962` for a `20.000` cavity.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe original pin failed before the production change:\n\n- `a_diamond_cavity_finish_is_generated_and_judged_clean`\n\nThe MCP pin covers schema discovery, translated outlines, generation, null clearing and early refusals:\n\n- `mcp_exposes_the_cavity_outline_and_burns_a_diamond_finish`\n\nThe ten motion pins pass:\n\n- `a_diamond_finish_is_judged_on_wall_offsets`\n- `matching_extents_do_not_hide_an_oversized_electrode_outline`\n- `a_finish_that_leaves_a_wall_undersize_is_refused`\n- `malformed_cavity_outlines_are_refused_by_name`\n- `an_excessive_cavity_outline_is_refused_before_geometry`\n- `a_cavity_outline_that_collapses_on_the_geometry_lattice_is_refused`\n- `cavity_outline_extents_must_match_the_stated_size`\n- `an_undersize_that_consumes_the_cavity_is_refused`\n- `a_small_electrode_cannot_hide_a_gap_that_burns_past_the_floor`\n- `a_vector_orbit_does_not_certify_angled_walls`\n\nEach mutation failed its pin with the old code or the guard removed.\nEach pin passed after restoration:\n\n- `old-generator`: red / green.\n- `shape-point-limit`: red / green.\n- `region-lattice`: red / green.\n- `extentmatch`: red / green.\n- `consumed-inset`: red / green.\n- `scalar-floor`: red / green.\n- `vector`: red / green.\n- `containment`: red / green.\n- `finish-coverage`: red / green.\n- `early-shape`: red / green.\n- `missing-electrode`: red / green.\n- `early-size`: red / green.\n\n## Refresh and validation\n\nThe branch merges `upstream/main` at `998c918bb04177c45a00396337b095e468acf4b8`.\nPR #2714 merged at `c9410977a`. This PR no longer requires a stack.\nMain's protected-item `cap: false` and conservative cylinder bound are retained.\n\nCurrent pins:\n\n- `a_stock_corner_inside_the_head_between_samples_blocks_the_plunge_and_the_retract`\n- `the_drawn_lollipop_is_the_whole_ball_united_with_the_neck`\n- `a_lifted_lollipop_ball_is_never_grown_smaller_than_its_solid`\n\nAuthor checks on `38f484aea`:\n\n- Quick gate: 693 steps, 0 failed, 39.6 minutes.\n- Clippy: clean for tools, sim, motion, app and ui, with `--all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n- Heavy gate: 241 steps, 0 failed, 28.7 minutes. Six known-fail steps were red as expected (#1950 and #2849).\n\nThe review trial merge also passed 695 quick steps and clippy.\nIts UI library rerun passed after the intermittent #2807 fault.\nThe review completed 37 motion heavy steps and 203 of 204 app heavy steps.\nBands 4 and 6 of `shared_face_bodies_finish` did not finish within the review command limit.\n\nThe diff against main changes no `.nc` or `.cl` golden.\nThe four undercut CL goldens are already in main through #2714.\n\nAuthor fix checks on `4ed23c5c7f3a5b53a8316604ea0e78cf4a4ae116`:\n\n- Restored end-to-end pins: `a_rounded_pockets_faces_yield_an_electrode_whose_burn_is_judged_clean` and `an_l_cavitys_electrode_keeps_its_notch_and_gouges_nothing`.\n- Both pins retain the outline refusal and then generate a box burn under the legacy extent law.\n- Rounded-pocket pin: gouge above 1 mm in a corner. L-cavity pin: gouge above 5 mm in the notch.\n- Remove both new outline clears: both pins RED at generation. Restore: seven suite tests GREEN.\n- Suppress rectangular electrode stock removal: both gouge checks RED. Restore: seven suite tests GREEN.\n- PR body content check: original RED, corrected GREEN.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 693 steps, zero failed, 108.1 minutes.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean, 3 minutes 33 seconds.\n- The gate ran with optional target seeding and sccache disabled after an initial cache-seed disk-quota failure.\n- This follow-up changes only the two existing test paths. No new heavy run was made.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe release gate and a real EDM control were not exercised.\nPositive-radius vector orbits with outlines are refused.\nTheir directions do not prove reach on angled walls.\nA round gap can still leave a recess at a sharp corner.\nThe wall law does not change that geometry or the stock tolerance.\nThe independent stock verdict judges the burn.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Sinker Burn judges stated cavity outlines on wall offsets, permits derived diamond finish electrodes, and refuses oversized electrodes by name. Undercut stock checks use exact disc-polygon intersection. Lollipop profiles draw the full ball united with the neck.\n\nFixes #1810\n\n\n",
